{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-01T15:36:42.784Z","data":{"text":"Task 1 complete.\n\n**Changed**\n- `src/core/report/stream-reads.ts` — new shared read scope built on `AsyncLocalStorage`:\n  - `withStreamReads` opens one scope; nested calls reuse the outer scope and the return value is the work's value.\n  - `readParsedFile` keyed by resolved absolute path + parser identity; caches the parsed promise so concurrent callers share one read and one object. Disk read via `fs.readFile(path, 'utf8')`; unreadable/missing → `null`; parser throw → rejection. No scope → always disk.\n  - `readEventStream` uses `parseEventLines`, drops `data.output` for `verify_ran`/`regressed`/`recertification`, and freezes every event and its `data`.\n- `tests/report-stream-reads.test.ts` — covers all acceptance lines, counting reads via `mock.method` on the default `node:fs/promises` export, and asserts the on-disk file still contains the removed logs.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/report-stream-reads.test.ts` → 11/11 pass.\n- `pnpm verify` → exit 0 (typechecks, build, all tests, lint).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/132-report-reads-once/.run/results/1.md`. Task 2 (routing report readers through the scope) is the noted next work."}}
